    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the welcome-notification feature for successful owner creation on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java`: a single-method OfficeFloor step that reads the saved `Owner` via `@Val` and emits a line on the `NOTIFY` logger containing the owner id and the memberId:\n```java\nNOTIFY.info(\"Welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n```\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted a `welcome` step between `audit` and `bulkWarning`. It runs after `save` (so `id` and `memberId` are populated) and carries `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors.\n\nModeled on the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` step, this keeps the notification side effect in its own step rather than in the responder, per the project's conventions.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`. The captured log confirms the line, e.g. `NOTIFY - Welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2616E6609E3`.",
